    "body": "**TLDR:** DeepSeek-V3, Kimi K2.5 and Kimi K3 turn on the `moe_dispatch` and `moe_combine` regions: one MoE layer, training fwd+bwd at 16k tokens per rank, EP 4, DeepSeek-V3 68.3 -> 52.4 ms (-23%), Kimi K2.5 -23%, Kimi K3 -16%. Reference path (Dist-MoE and DeepEP have their own dispatch and combine), low priority.\n\n**Stack** (6 PRs, merge bottom-up; this PR is in **bold**)\n\n| # | PR | Independent? | Needs (stack positions) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | AllToAll dispatcher: permute and unpermute with gathers | yes | — |\n| 2 | Argsort expert ids on the narrowest integer type | yes | — |\n| 3 | EP=1 inference: gather-sum MoE combine region | no | 2 |\n| 4 | EP=1 inference: sort-region MoE dispatch | no | 2, 3 |\n| 5 | Gather-sum dispatch and combine for training, at any EP | no | 4 |\n| **6** | **Turn on gather-sum dispatch and combine for DeepSeek-V3 and Kimi** | **no** | **3, 4, 5** |\n\n**Problem**\n1. **Opt-in.** The gather-sum dispatch and combine run only for models whose `local_compile_regions` list `moe_dispatch` and `moe_combine`.\n2. **Who lists them.** Only `Qwen35Model.Config`.\n3. **DeepSeek-V3 and Kimi instead.** The eager combine: an fp32 multiply and a scatter-add; the token gather's backward is an accumulating `index_put`.\n4. **Cost.** 16 of the 68 ms of a DeepSeek-V3 MoE layer fwd+bwd (Results).\n\n**Solution**\n1. Add `\"moe_dispatch\"` and `\"moe_combine\"` to `DeepSeekV3Model.Config.local_compile_regions` and `KimiK3Model.Config.local_compile_regions`.\n2. Kimi K2.5 gets them through `KimiK25Model.Config`, which subclasses `DeepSeekV3Model.Config`.\n3. **Reaches** `deepseek_v3_671b` (EP 2, all-to-all) and the DeepSeek-V3 / Kimi test recipes that don't use the SPMD typechecker.\n4. **Not reached:** the three NVFP4 recipes, which set `[\"loss\"]`.\n5. Unchanged: eager runs, recipes that set their own region list, and the DeepEP, HybridEP and Dist-MoE dispatchers.\n\n**Results**\n```text\nNumerics: not bitwise. The compiled combine and token-gather backward sum a token's routes in fp32 and round once; eager rounds per route.\nmax rel L2 vs fp64, op level (CPU probe); bf16 rounding floor 1.66e-3\nop                                          eager      compiled\ncombine (top-8 and top-16)                  2.34e-3    1.66e-3\ntoken-gather backward, top-8 (DSv3, K2.5)   3.68e-3    1.66e-3\ntoken-gather backward, top-16 (Kimi K3)     5.02e-3    1.66e-3\nBoth arms bitwise identical run to run (2 processes each).\n\none MoE layer (ffn_norm + MoE), training fwd+bwd, 16k tokens per rank, FSDP 4 + EP 4, all-to-all dispatcher, no activation\ncheckpointing, 4x GB300, native dims, random weights and routing, the model's other default regions on in both arms,\nCUDA-event ms per step (mean of 3 steps), mean [range] of 2 alternating processes per arm\nmodel              before               after                delta    peak GiB\nDeepSeek-V3 671B   68.3 [67.8-68.8]     52.4 [52.3-52.5]     -23.3%   40.2 -> 38.6\nKimi K2.5          70.0 [69.5-70.4]     53.6 [53.2-54.0]     -23.4%   54.7 -> 54.7\nKimi K3            96.4 [96.3-96.6]     81.1 [80.6-81.5]     -15.9%   89.9 -> 89.9\ngraphs: +4 (one per compiled training dispatch / combine function, DeepSeek-V3); none recompile when routing changes every step; limit 8\n\nafter vs before, rank 0, max rel L2 (bitwise = identical); \"2 routed\" = the first 2 of the 64 / 96 / 224 local experts\nmodel              output    input grad   router grad   expert weight grads             other grads\nDeepSeek-V3 671B   3.4e-3    3.3e-3       1.5e-7        bitwise (shared + 2 routed)     ffn_norm 3.9e-3\nKimi K2.5          3.6e-3    3.4e-3       1.5e-7        bitwise (shared + 2 routed)     ffn_norm 4.1e-3\nKimi K3            3.4e-3    3.6e-3       1.1e-3        shared bitwise, routed 3.0e-3   ffn_norm, routed_down / norm / up 6.1e-3\n\ndeepseek_v3_debugmodel, 1 GPU, EP 1, training CUDA graphs on, the recipe's activation checkpointing, seeded, 10 steps\ngraph: forward_backward recorded once, with both regions inside; no errors, losses finite\nloss       before     after\nstep 1     8.06955    8.06956\nstep 10    3.73792    3.73786\nmax |d| over 10 steps: 1.0e-4 (same code, run to run: 3.0e-4; cuDNN attention is not deterministic)\n```\nExpert weight grads are bitwise for DeepSeek-V3 and Kimi K2.5 because the combine's output grad is the same in both arms.\n\nYou may ask: why one training size per model? The shared code was measured across token counts and in inference on Qwen3.5 in stack positions 3-5; only the per-model flip is new here.\n\nNOTE:\n- Needs stack position 5, which registers both names; on main alone `apply_local_compile` raises \"Unknown local_compile_regions entries\".\n- Kimi K3: the combine feeds `routed_norm` and `routed_up`, so expert and router grads change; an RMSNorm backward turns the combine's difference into 7.6e-4 on the per-route grad (CPU probe); the growth to 3.0e-3 is not isolated.\n- `deepseek_v3_fsdp+ep` and `deepseek_v3_fsdp+cp+pp+ep` compare exact losses to golden files this PR changes. Before landing, regenerate `real_pg/a10g/deepseek_v3.txt` and `deepseek_v3_cp_pp.txt` (integration workflow, `export_results` dispatch), `fake_pg/a10g/deepseek_v3.txt` (the Fake-PG job, which that dispatch does not run) and the two `real_pg/mi350x/` files (ROCm CI, no export dispatch).\n- Not run: a full-size training step or loss curve, EP 8, TP > 1, PP and full-size activation checkpointing (`deepseek_v3_671b` uses both), MXFP8 / NVFP4 (at EP > 1 their dispatcher goes through the same all-to-all combine), H100, inference for these models, the smaller DeepSeek-V3 and Kimi flavors.\n\n**Test plan**\n```bash\npytest tests/unit_tests/cpu/models/kimi_k3/ tests/unit_tests/cpu/models/deepseek_v3/ tests/unit_tests/cpu/models/common/test_token_dispatcher.py tests/unit_tests/cpu/models/common/test_moe.py\n# 53 passed\n```\nLayer timing and numerics: a local script (not in the PR) builds each model's first MoE layer with FSDP 4 + EP 4 and diffs rank 0's output and grads.\n",
